  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#21313\", \"PowerToys#33581\", \"PowerToys#29382\"], \"answer\": \"This feature has been requested several times before, so PowerToys has no keyboard cleaning mode. The main tracking ticket is PowerToys#21313, a request for a utility that disables the keyboard, mouse and touchscreen while you clean them. Your ticket is a duplicate of it, as are #33581, #29382 and #20445. The PowerToys team said they have no plans to build this (#21313, #28596). Their suggestion was to lock the PC with Win+L or shut it down. Other workarounds from the tickets: unplug a USB keyboard, or turn off Bluetooth or take the batteries out of a wireless one. On a laptop you can open Device Manager (Win+X), go to Keyboards, and disable the internal keyboard (#44783). Then re-enable it afterwards. A third-party keyboard-lock tool is another option. If you want the feature, add a thumbs-up to #21313 instead of opening a new ticket.\"}",
